    {
      "@id": "#claim",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "name": "Entry 43: the fifth rider set — the frozen law on four European riders (D6)",
      "text": "Yes, and it reaches its closest parity there: on D6's 740 clean rides from four European riders, F3 with ε_d reads 3.16% against the simulation's 3.15%. The same corpus breaks F4's scalar c while leaving the form intact — the sharpest available evidence that c belongs to the elevation source rather than to cycling. Its riders pedal descents far more than the ultra-distance specialists, confirmed physics-free from descent occupancy, which does not embarrass the deficit but explains it.",
      "appearance": [
        {
          "@id": "https://github.com/danlessa/bicycling-energy-model/blob/main/research/journal/MODEL_COMPARISON_JOURNAL.md"
        }
      ],
      "subjectOf": {
        "@id": "https://github.com/danlessa/bicycling-energy-model/blob/main/research/notes/claims.ttl"
      }
    },
